;; incremental-elab-loses-span-file-provenance (diagnostic half): a type error
;; under `--interpret` must be reported against THIS file at its own 1-based
;; line, not against the synthetic `<eval>` blob at a line offset by however
;; many prelude `(load ...)` lines happened to be accumulated first.
;;
;; The expected.diag needles below pin the path and the line together, which is
;; what makes this a provenance test rather than another type-mismatch test --
;; before the fix the interpreter reported `<eval>:64:10` here while the
;; compiled path reported the real location all along.
;;
;; Kept deliberately dull: the error itself is the plainest possible mismatch,
;; so the fixture fails only if the LOCATION regresses.
(defn main [] : int
  (let [x 1]
    (+ x "boom")))
